Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.75,0:00:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What happens when a peaceful
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.07,0:00:04.41,Default,,0,0,0,,lake suddenly erupts into fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.11,0:00:07.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Taal Volcano, a small island
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.28,0:00:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,in a Philippine lake, sits
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.96,0:00:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,on the Pacific Ring of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire, where converging plates
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.91,0:00:13.82,Default,,0,0,0,,fuel violent eruptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.12,0:00:14.92,Default,,0,0,0,,On the afternoon of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.92,0:00:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,12 January 2020, seismic swarms
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.92,0:00:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,began at eleven a.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.68,0:00:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,m.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.81,0:00:22.23,Default,,0,0,0,,, and by one p.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.53,0:00:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,m.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.66,0:00:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,a phreatomagmatic blast ripped
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.82,0:00:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,through the main crater, sending
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.91,0:00:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,ash and steam skyward.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.48,0:00:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The explosion hurled a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.62,0:00:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,hundred‑meter ash column,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.39,0:00:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,darkened Manila’s sky, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.17,0:00:36.44,Default,,0,0,0,,forced officials to raise the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.44,0:00:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,alert to level four, the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.08,0:00:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,highest warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.65,0:00:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Ash fell across Calabarzon,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.77,0:00:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,schools closed, flights halted,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.27,0:00:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and the once‑blue crater lake
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.82,0:00:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,temporarily dried, erasing the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.99,0:00:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,tiny Vulcan Point island.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.11,0:00:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Smaller eruptions returned in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.77,0:00:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,July 2021 and again in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.90,0:00:56.40,Default,,0,0,0,,March 2022, each prompting a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.40,0:00:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,temporary jump to alert level
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.08,0:01:00.08,Default,,0,0,0,,three as scientists monitored
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.08,0:01:02.45,Default,,0,0,0,,renewed magma‑water interaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.75,0:01:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,These brief but fierce outbursts
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.79,0:01:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,illustrate how water meeting
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.11,0:01:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,magma creates explosive power
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.25,0:01:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,that can reshape a landscape
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.84,0:01:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,in minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.37,0:01:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, Taal’s calm surface
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.19,0:01:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,reminds us that even the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.80,0:01:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,smallest volcano can unleash
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.27,0:01:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Earth’s restless interior at
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.06,0:01:19.03,Default,,0,0,0,,any moment.